    <summary>Opinionated CLI utility to organize music by metadata</summary>
    <description>
# muxic

An opinionated command-line music organizer. Copies or moves audio files from a
source directory into a clean `Artist/Album/TrackNum - Title.ext` hierarchy,
driven entirely by each file's ID3 tags.

- Recursively scans a source directory and organizes by embedded metadata
- Copy or move, with a dry-run mode
- Windows-safe filename sanitization (Unicode transliteration, reserved chars, title casing)
- Duplicate detection via SHA-256 signatures
- FLAC-over-MP3 upgrade when a better copy exists

## Supported formats

MP3, FLAC, and other tagged audio formats supported by the underlying tag reader.
    </description>
